# Runtime configuration for fridged. Installed to /etc/default/fridged.
#
# THIS IS THE FILE YOU EDIT to swap a simulated part for a real one. The systemd
# unit never changes; after editing here:
#
#     sudo systemctl restart fridged
#     journalctl -u fridged -f
#
# Not in git once installed: it is machine-local, and the copy in deploy/ is a
# template.

# Where the database lives. Must match the path in the Grafana datasource
# (grafana/provisioning/datasources/sqlite.yml), and must be a directory the
# `grafana` group can write — see the note about WAL in fridged.service.
FRIDGE_DB=/var/lib/fridge/fridge.db

# Arguments to `python3 -m fridged`.
#
# Swap ONE THING AT A TIME and confirm it before the next, so a failure has one
# possible cause instead of three. The intended order is in deploy/README.md:
#
#   1. the board      --port sim          ->  --port /dev/serial/by-id/...
#   2. the camera     (simulated shelf)   ->  --camera picapture
#   3. card payments  --square fake       ->  --square real
#
# USE THE by-id PATH, NOT /dev/ttyACM0. The number is assigned in the order
# devices are enumerated, so it moves when the board is replugged or reset while
# the Pi is up — which is most of the time during testing. The by-id path is
# derived from the RP2040's serial number and never changes. Find yours with:
#
#     ls -l /dev/serial/by-id/
#
# Camera moved AHEAD of payments compared with the original order, because it is
# the one that can fail on permissions: the service runs with Group=grafana and
# only the supplementary groups fridged.service names. Confirm the camera works
# under systemd before adding real money to the picture.
#
# Simulated board, busy enough to watch:
FRIDGED_ARGS=--port sim --sim-activity 30 --square fake

# The real fridge. Substitute your own by-id path — the serial number is the
# board's, not transferable:
# FRIDGED_ARGS=--port /dev/serial/by-id/usb-Raspberry_Pi_Pico_E46570978F401029-if00 --camera picapture --square real
